### Quoted specification text

Rumoca cites the Modelica Language Specification extensively and quotes short
excerpts from it, in `crates/rumoca-contracts/data/formal_statements.toml` and
in `spec/SPEC_0022_MLS_COMPILER_COMPLIANCE.md`. The Modelica Language
Specification is Copyright the Modelica Association, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0.
Every excerpt is short, is attributed to its section, and is quoted rather than
adapted. The same applies to the FMI and eFMI specification sections cited in
the FMI and GALEC crates.

### Tools invoked but not redistributed

The verification and benchmark rigs invoke external tools as separate
processes and record their digests as measurement provenance: OpenModelica
(OSMC-PL), QEMU and the GNU Arm toolchain (GPL), and CasADi (LGPL-3.0), the
last of these through Python code that Rumoca emits and that the user's own
environment resolves. None is linked into, vendored by, or redistributed with
any Rumoca artifact, so no copyleft term reaches this repository or its
binaries. C code generated by CasADi carries CasADi's own banner stating that
the generated content is not copyrighted and that the copied runtime templates
are MIT-0; that banner is the license record and must never be stripped from a
generated file.

